[critique] wave 0 plan: revise
[directions] d-13 [open] Deepen weakest claim 1: Lyman-alpha thermal-relic bound m_th; d-14 [open] Deepen weakest claim 2: DW sterile-neutrino mass mapping m_s; d-15 [open] Background literature check: mixed cold+warm DM loophole and
**Plan.** Three lines of investigation.

1. Deepen weakest claim 1: Lyman-alpha thermal-relic bound m_th >5.3-5.7 keV robustness to IGM thermal history priors and emulator systematics. Prior board (d-02, d-08) verified m_th limits only at abstract/snippet level with no citable quotes for k_max cuts, T0(z)/gamma priors, pressure smoothing, mean flux, or patchy reionization, and no quantitative LaCE vs Lyssa vs Sherwood-Relics emulator comparison. This is the core small-scale structure probe claim and most prior-dependent.
2. Deepen weakest claim 2: DW sterile-neutrino mass mapping m_s=4.43 keV (m_th/1keV)^{4/3} and X-ray vs Lyman-alpha binding constraint on f_s=1. Prior board (d-03, d-05, d-06, d-07) left Viel 2005 Eq.5 coefficient unverified against full text, no second mapping (Abazajian/half-mode/2007.13751) spread quantified, tool Omega_s h^2 normalization 3-16x higher than published DW formulas unresolved, and X-ray sin^2(2theta) limits not digitized so f_s,max_Xray and binding constraint per mass (7.1,20,22,29,45 keV) missing.
3. Background literature check: mixed cold+warm DM loophole and Planck/BBN complementarity to pure WDM bound. Brief highlights CWDM (cold+warm fraction) reopening keV-scale space and tension with 0.6-1.6 keV warmness claims; prior board extracted 0812.0010 and 2504.06367 fraction bounds but did not digitize curves or check Planck N_eff/Yp/D/H shifts from sterile thermalization.

The critic asked for changes:
- Steps do not read SCOPE.md / ISSUES.md / prior references.bib via read_text_file to systematically identify weakest claims; add board audit before literature fetch to avoid repeating d-02/d-08.
- Success criteria requires table for 1306.2314, 1702.01764, 2209.14220, 2309.04533 but steps only fetch 2309.04533 and 1702.01764; add web_search/read_arxiv_chunk for 1306.2314 and 2209.14220 or narrow criteria.
- Emulator error propagation to m_th (keV shift) risks unverifiable claim; restrict to quote-verified leave-one-out errors and prior-dependence statements from LaCE 2011.15127/2305.19064 and Sherwood-Relics 2504.06367, do not infer shift without quoted mapping.
