**Blocked — Deepen weakest claim 2: DW sterile-neutrino mass mapping m_s=4.43 keV (m_th/1keV)^{4/3} and X-ray vs Lyman-alpha binding constraint on f_s=1.** Tool budget reached (5 calls used) before completing Viel 2005 and Abazajian 2006 full-text reads, before quantifying tool vs published normalization factor, and before digitizing X-ray limit curves; get_paper_figures for 2207.04572 failed (no HTML rendering, PDF-only tikz figures), and web searches for equation texts timed out, leaving success criteria unmet. Direction d-14 asked to deepen the Dodelson-Widrow (non-resonant production) sterile-neutrino mass mapping and the X-ray versus Lyman-alpha binding constraint for 100% sterile-neutrino dark matter. What was established: the sterile-neutrino server models DW and Shi-Fuller resonant (SF, with lepton asymmetry L) production, with Big Bang Nucleosynthesis (BBN, light-element abundances Yp and D/H) fit valid for N_eff 2.044-6.044 and m_s below ~100 keV. A DW grid at sin^2(2theta)=1e-12 gave Omega_s h^2 (relic density in units of critical density) 0.00047 at 7.1 keV, 0.00304 at 20 keV, 0.00361 at 22 keV, 0.00594 at 29 keV, 0.0131 at 45 keV, implying f_s=1 (100% dark matter) mixings 2.5e-10, 3.9e-11, 3.3e-11, 2.0e-11, 9.2e-12 respectively (for observed Omega_DM h^2=0.12), with Delta N_eff 6e-6 to 2.7e-5 and BBN Delta chi^2 ~0 (allowed). File: /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-lyman-wdm/runs/261107_185835/sterile_nu_grid_DW_bc0526.csv. The 3.5 keV line benchmark (m_s=7.1 keV, sin^2 2theta=7e-11, DW) produces Delta N_eff=0.00043 (N_eff=3.0444), Omega_s h^2=0.033 (27.5% of dark matter), Yp=0.2468 (observed 0.2449 +/-0.004) and D/H=2.44e-5 (observed 2.547 +/-0.025e-5) with BBN Delta chi^2=-0.01 (allowed), photon energy E=m_s/2=3.55 keV, radiative lifetime 5.8e27 s (1.8e20 yr), free-streaming length 151 kpc, and is flagged excluded by NuSTAR M31 (Roach+2020) and XMM-Newton blank sky (Dessert+2020) in the tool's 10-limit database. A contrasting SF grid at same masses and mixing gave Omega_s h^2 6.17 to 248, all overclosing by 50-2000x, with heuristic Delta N_eff 0.1x DW (6e-7 to 2.7e-6). File: /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-lyman-wdm/runs/261107_185835/sterile_nu_grid_SF_ec8837.csv. Roach et al. 2022 (arXiv:2207.04572) NuSTAR Milky Way halo search with ~7 Ms/detector blank-sky exposures sets sin^2(2theta) limits for m_s 6-40 keV, strongly disfavors the 7 keV 3.5 keV line, and derives leading limits at 15-18 keV and 25-40 keV reaching below the BBN limit. No figures were digitized. What remains open: quote-verified Viel 2005 (astro-ph/0501562) Eq.5 coefficient 4.43 keV and alpha(m_x) formula with file offsets, Abazajian 2006 Eq.7 and hep-ph/0612182 Sec.7.1 alternative normalizations, quantitative tool versus published Omega_s h^2 normalization factor (3-16x) at 5 masses, digitized X-ray sin^2 limits at 7.1,20,22,29,45 keV with f_s,max_Xray and binding constraint per mass (X-ray vs Lyman-alpha mixed-DM F_wdm<0.35 and f_WDM<0.16-0.67), mapping spread in keV and percent between Viel, Abazajian, and half-mode matchings, and full citation of 2207.04572 with verbatim quotes. All compute ran locally; no facility dispatch was used.
