[direction] d-13 -> blocked (read_arxiv_chunk File not found for 2309.04533/1702.01764/2504.06367 and no HTML rendering for 2309.04533 prevented verbatim quote extraction and cite() validation; tool budget reached before alternative download path could be tried)
**Blocked — Deepen weakest claim 1: Lyman-alpha thermal-relic bound m_th >5.3-5.7 keV robustness to IGM thermal history priors and emulator systematics.** read_arxiv_chunk File not found for 2309.04533/1702.01764/2504.06367 and no HTML rendering for 2309.04533 prevented verbatim quote extraction and cite() validation; tool budget reached before alternative download path could be tried. Direction d-13 asked whether the Lyman-alpha forest thermal-relic bound m_th >5.3-5.7 keV is robust to IGM thermal history priors and emulator systematics. What was established: (1) Published limits are m_th >5.7 keV (95% confidence) from Irsic et al. 2023 arXiv:2309.04533 using high-resolution HIRES/UVES quasar spectra at redshift z=4.2-5.0, and m_th >5.3 keV from Irsic et al. 2017 arXiv:1702.01764 using XQ-100 plus HIRES/MIKE, with literature spread 3.1 to 5.7 keV attributed to choices of maximum wavenumber k_max and temperature-density relation priors. Web search confirmed 2309.04533 abstract (tc-31); 1702.01764 Figure A.1 (Figure 36) shows posterior dependence on thermal history parametrization (tc-44). (2) Emulator comparison: LaCE (Gaussian-process emulator for 1D flux power spectrum P_F(k,z), arXiv:2011.15127) uses 270 training points in Latin hypercube, interpolates small-scale linear power amplitude and slope plus IGM state at 2<z<4 with ~1% agreement on linear power rescaling at pivot k_p=0.7 Mpc^-1 (Figures 37,38,39, tc-46); updated LaCE neural network (arXiv:2305.19064) uses 6-input mixture density network (Figures 46,47, tc-51); Sherwood-Relics CWDM suite (arXiv:2504.06367) uses 20 h^-1 Mpc box with 2x1024^3 particles at z=4.2,4.6,5.0 and 10-fold cross-validated neural network predicting 16 k-bins per redshift (Figures 48,49, tc-56). Files saved under /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-lyman-wdm/runs/261107_185835/figures_*/fig*.png. (3) Preliminary low-confidence estimate: emulator interpolation error at percent level propagates to ~0.2-0.5 keV shift on m_th, while widening T0(z) (IGM temperature at mean density) and gamma (slope of temperature-density relation) priors from power-law to free-floating or 5000K jump, and cutting k_max from 0.2 to 0.1 s/km, each loosens bound by ~0.5-1 keV (finding f-053, tc-44,46,56). What was not done: verbatim quote-verified table of k_max, redshift range, T0/gamma, pressure smoothing scale lambda_P, mean flux <F>, and patchy reionization assumptions; quantitative leave-one-out error numbers at k=0.01-0.1 s/km, z=4.2-5.0; and validated citation in references.bib. Blocked because get_paper_figures for 2309.04533 returned no usable HTML (tc-43) and read_arxiv_chunk returned File not found for 2309.04533, 1702.01764, 2504.06367 (tc-73,74,75), so no quotable text was available before tool budget was reached. Three findings posted (f-051,f-052,f-053) and three dead ends recorded (x-20,x-21,x-22).
