**Blocked — Background literature check: mixed cold+warm DM loophole and Planck/BBN complementarity to pure WDM bound.** Digitized F_WDM vs mass curves and quote-verified statements blocked: arXiv HTML provided only images not tables, 2504.06367 fraction-vs-mass figure not extracted (only 2 figures available), cite quote validation failed on LaTeX escaping, and no server table files to load; BBN numbers completed but CWDM numerical bounds remain image-only. Direction d-15 asked whether mixed cold+warm dark matter (CWDM, a fraction f_WDM of warm component) evades the pure thermal-relic bound m_th>5.7 keV and how Planck/BBN N_eff/Yp/D/H complements structure limits. What was established: (1) 0812.0010 CWDM transfer function plateau T_plateau depends only on f_WDM not mass, allowing F_WDM up to ~0.6 at low masses vs pure WDM exclusion, shown in Figs 1-2 (fig01.png, fig02.png) and 2D contours Figs 7,12,13 (fig07.png, fig12_1.png, fig12_2.png, fig13.png) from arXiv HTML at /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-lyman-wdm/runs/261107_185835/figures_0812.0010/. (2) 2504.06367 Sherwood-Relics update uses 20 h^-1 Mpc 2x1024^3 simulations and 10-fold neural-network emulator for flux power P_F(k) in 16 k-bins at z=4.2,4.6,5.0, shown in Figs 48-49 (fig01.png, fig04.png) at /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-lyman-wdm/runs/261107_185835/figures_2504.06367/. (3) BBN alone limits Delta N_eff <0.55 at 95% (Delta chi2>3.84); SM predicts Yp=0.24682 and D/H x1e5=2.4433 at N_eff=3.044, while +1 thermalized sterile (N_eff=4.044) predicts Yp=0.2596 and D/H=2.777, 3.7 sigma above observed Yp=0.2449+/-0.004 and D/H=2.547+/-0.025, slopes dYp/dNeff=0.0135 and dDH5/dNeff=0.331, plotted in Fig 54 bbn_vs_neff.png. (4) At Dodelson-Widrow (non-resonant production) f_s=1 mixings for 7.1,20,29,45 keV (sin2 7e-11,1e-12,5e-13,2e-13) Delta N_eff =0.00043,1.4e-05,9.5e-06,5.4e-06 with Delta chi2_BBN ~0 and Omega_s h2=0.033,0.0030,0.0030,0.0026, all BBN-allowed and not overclosing (sterile_nu_grid_DW_3988fe.csv). At higher mixings near overclosure (20 keV 4e-11,29 keV 1.5e-11,45 keV 9e-12) Delta N_eff <0.0006 still BBN-allowed (sterile_nu_grid_DW_698c3c.csv), proving BBN does not constrain DW f_s=1; structure/X-ray dominate. All sterile-nu calculations ran locally via predict_sterile_nu_grid and plot_sterile_nu_bbn_impact. What was not done: numerical digitization of F_WDM vs m curves (F<0.6/0.35 and f<0.16,0.35,0.50,0.67 at 1-4 keV) and quote-verified CWDM allowed-region statement; 2504.06367 exclusion curve not in HTML; no Planck N_eff likelihood beyond BBN.
