**After wave 1.** d-13 and d-14 are the two weakest claims (low-confidence emulator error propagation and unverified DW mapping/X-ray binding) and their blockers (File not found, tool budget, no HTML rendering) are removable with cached-file listing and remaining 14-call budget; d-15 is closed as sufficiently supported on CWDM plateau and BBN Delta N_eff<0.55 with remaining digitization low priority. Two new directions each provide a contrasting emulator/tool call (LaCE vs Sherwood-Relics and DW vs SF plus X-ray line) and one new paper with verbatim quotes (Irsic 2023 2309.04533 and Roach 2022 2207.04572) to post corrected findings before report, keeping compute local per q-05 as 400-point grids do not require facility dispatch.

New directions:
- Quantify Lyman-alpha m_th >5.3-5.7 keV robustness to IGM thermal history priors and emulator systematics with contrasting LaCE vs Sherwood-Relics emulators and quote-verified Irsic 2023/2017.
- Resolve DW sterile-neutrino mass mapping normalization and X-ray vs Lyman-alpha binding constraint on f_s=1 with contrasting DW vs SF tool calls and digitized Roach 2022 NuSTAR limits.
