**Blocked — Quantify Lyman-alpha m_th >5.3-5.7 keV robustness to IGM thermal history priors and emulator systematics with contrasting LaCE vs Sherwood-Relics emulators and quote-verified Irsic 2023/2017.** Tool budget exhausted before get_paper_figures, read_arxiv_chunk, cite, predict_sterile_nu_grid, or scan_sterile_nu_parameters could run (tc-106); no cached PDFs for 2309.04533, 1702.01764, 2504.06367 in runs/261107_185835 (only 0812.0010.pdf present, tc-91) and list_input_files empty (tc-92), so verbatim quotes and quantitative emulator error extraction were impossible. Direction d-16 asked whether the Lyman-alpha forest thermal-relic bound m_th >5.3-5.7 keV is robust to IGM thermal history priors and emulator systematics. What was established in this wave: Irsic et al. 2023 (arXiv:2309.04533) reports m_th >5.7 keV (95% confidence) from high-resolution HIRES/UVES at redshift z=4.2-5.0 and Irsic et al. 2017 (arXiv:1702.01764) reports m_th >5.3 keV from XQ-100 plus HIRES/MIKE, with literature spread 3.1 to 5.7 keV attributed to maximum wavenumber k_max cut and temperature-density relation T0(z) and gamma prior choices (web search tc-99 confirms 2309.04533 abstract). LaCE Gaussian-process emulator (arXiv:2011.15127, 270 Latin hypercube points, ~1% linear power rescaling accuracy) versus Sherwood-Relics neural-network emulator (arXiv:2504.06367, 20 h^-1 Mpc box with 2x1024^3 particles, 16 k-bins at z=4.2,4.6,5.0, 10-fold cross-validation) comparison remains at architecture level from prior run figures in /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-lyman-wdm/runs/261107_185835/figures_*/. Preliminary low-confidence estimate that percent-level flux power P_F(k,z) interpolation error propagates to 0.2-0.5 keV shift on m_th and that widening T0/gamma priors from power-law to free-floating or 5000K jump and cutting k_max from 0.2 to 0.1 s/km each loosen bound by 0.5-1 keV remains unverified. What was not done: verbatim quote-verified table of k_max, z range, T0/gamma, pressure smoothing lambda_P, mean flux <F>, patchy reionization with cite() entries; quantitative leave-one-out error at k=0.01-0.1 s/km, z=4.2-5.0 in percent and propagated keV shift; contrasting LaCE vs Sherwood-Relics P_F predictions. No new compute ran on facility; all checks were local file listings and web search. Three findings posted (f-066, f-067, f-068) and one dead end recorded (x-25). Open questions q-11, q-12, q-13 remain.
